      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Level: use June's 47.5398 percent persistence anchor, close to both reference-class means. Momentum: add zero because recent changes alternate in sign. Cohort effect: the June-to-August 2025 increase was 5.4625 percentage points; apply an analyst-selected 25 percent weight because a single prior summer provides weak seasonal evidence. One-off and policy-mechanism adjustments: add zero without verified evidence of a new Kansas implementation. CMS explains that automation completed after a form is sent can be classified as form-based renewal, making reported ex parte shares sensitive to workflow."
