        "text": "Prior/update/interval: Persistence prior with a weak summer-cohort adjustment; historical sample is 13 unrounded Kansas O shares, June 2025\u2013June 2026. Point = 47.539765 + 0.25*(43.860711-38.398202) + 0 momentum + 0 one-off + 0 policy = 48.905392, rounded to 48.9 percent. The 12 successive changes are -2.3933, 7.8558, 4.7405, 6.8451, 0.6159, -2.6599, -8.2490, 0.5646, 5.4042, -4.3685, -0.5787 and 1.3648 percentage points; their mean is 0.761797. Sample sigma = 4.825222 percentage points, computed as sqrt(sum((change-0.761797)^2)/11). The approximate Gaussian 80 percent one-month half-width is 1.28*sigma = 6.176284 points. For the two-month June-to-August horizon, assuming independent monthly innovations, multiply by sqrt(2): half-width = 8.734584. Unrounded bounds are 40.170808 and 57.639977 percent; final bounds are 40.2 and 57.6 percent."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Upside risk: an August cohort with more readily verified income records or improved automatic matching raises ex parte renewals. Downside risk: matching failures, more complex cases or renewals classified as form-based reduce the share. A substantial automation improvement could land above 57.6 percent, outside the interval; a disrupted renewal batch or markedly less matchable cohort could land below 40.2 percent, outside the interval. The single prior summer may reflect transitional processing rather than repeatable seasonality."
